SUMMARY:In The Other Room: Eric Freedman
LOCATION:Portland
DESCRIPTION:Eric delivers sharp\, dark\, and brutally honest comedy that cu
 ts through the noise with precision. A former punk/hardcore drummer\, and R
 oad Manager for Sublime With Rome\, Eric has spent most of his adult life t
 ouring the world collecting the kind of wild stories most people would leav
 e out of a job interview. Some of his material has been called "tragically 
 accurate\," which\, honestly\, sounds about right.\n\nAfter three years on 
 the road opening for comedian Craig Conant\, Eric has ventured off on his o
 wn to headline clubs and bars around the country. He performs regularly at 
 L.A.'s big three comedy clubs: The Hollywood Improv\, The Comedy Store\, an
 d The Laugh Factory\, and you can listen to his debut comedy album "Eric Di
 dn't Go To College" on all music platforms.\n\nEric is also known as one of
  the minds behind the cult animation group\, Tomorrow's Nobody\, where he's
  collaborated on cartoons with many top comedians including Tom Segura\, Th
 eo Von\, Adam Ray\, Drew Lynch\, Craig Conant\, & Shapel Lacey. His videos 
 have garnered over 100 million views.\n\nThere is a two-item per person min
 imum in the Showroom\, which can be fulfilled with any food or drink items 
 from the menu.\n\nPLEASE NOTE: Food and drinks purchased in the bar and lou
 nge do not count towards the two-item minimum.\n\nManagement reserves the r
 ight to prevent customers from entering the facility who they deem disrupti
 ve or dangerous to other patrons.\nMore info: https://comedyatlas.app/comed
 y-atlas/event/in-the-other-room-eric-freedman/
